gesting a modest continuation of the downtrend rather than an accelerated selloff."}, "news": {"predicted_close": 247.2, "direction": "up", "confidence": 0.72, "rationale": "A U.S.-Iran peace deal drove Nasdaq 100 futures up ~2% and broadly lifted risk sentiment, while AMZN's deeply oversold RSI (26.76), strong analyst consensus (Strong Buy, avg PT $308), Prime Day anticipation, and fresh AWS/AI catalysts all support a meaningful bounce from the prior close of $238.55."}}, "rationale": "Momentum and macro are the only strategies with any directional wins (0.5 hit rate, lowest MAPEs) and both call a modest continuation lower; I lean on them but cap any single weight per the failure note about over-tilting. Technical, contrarian, and news have 0/2 hit rates and the news up-call (247.2) is an overconfident outlier I distrust, so they get minimal weight. Strategies disagree on sign, so I lower confidence and keep the prediction close to the prior-close anchor with only a mild downward tilt.", "quote_source": "alphavantage", "status": "pending", "actual_close": null}
